## What an Awards Ceremony Needs From the Audiovisual Side

A ceremony asks different things from the equipment than a conference. In a conference one person speaks for a long time. In a ceremony many people speak for a short time, one after another, and the gaps between them are as important as the speeches. That changes what you need:

-   **A microphone for the host that is always on and a way for each winner to be heard.** Winners usually speak briefly, and a microphone that is passed from hand to hand is the usual answer.
-   **Light on the place where people stand.** The audience should see the winner's face, not only a silhouette.
-   **A screen with the names or the category.** It tells the room who is next while the host reads.
-   **A person who knows the system.** A fault in the middle of a ceremony is seen by everyone.

## Microphones for the Host and the Winners

The host is on stage for the whole ceremony, so a microphone that stays with them, held or on a stand, covers most of it. The winners need a microphone when they reach the stage. The usual setups are a second handheld that the host passes along, or a gooseneck microphone on a [lectern](/blog/lectern-rental/) where each winner steps up and speaks.

We own six wireless handheld microphones, all Audix, and our [guide to wireless handheld microphone rental](/blog/wireless-handheld-microphone-rental/) explains which package carries one and how extra ones are quoted. The MICE Pack includes one handheld and one gooseneck, so a host on the handheld and winners at a gooseneck on a lectern are covered by the package's microphones, with the lectern as an extra at 50 euros. A second handheld is an add on by quote. If your winners talk from their seats, a handheld that is carried to them is the other common setup, and it needs somebody to carry it.

## Lighting the Stage

The stage has to be lit so the faces can be seen from the back of the room. Our own lighting inventory is small and honest. We own 2 Eurolite LED KLS-200 light bars, 1 ADJ Encore FRI50Z Fresnel wash light and 1 ADJ Element H6 Pack of 6 wireless uplights. The Fresnel is the one that washes a person or a podium in even light, and the uplights add color to a wall or a backdrop from the floor. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) also includes 2 RGBW light bars.

Our lighting has no DMX control: the Eurolite bars run on a foot pedal and the other fixtures are fixed and set up by our crew. We do not have moving head fixtures or programmable automated rigs, so we do not offer light shows with moving beams. Our [guide to stage lighting rental](/blog/stage-lighting-rental/) lists every fixture with what it does. Anything beyond that, such as a lighting rig or an overhead truss, is not in our own inventory, and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one.

