## Screen, Music and Cues

The MICE Pack includes a 60 inch LED display, which is enough to show a category and a name to a room of up to 120 guests. For a bigger room, tell us the layout and we say what we can supply and what we would source. We do not have a video wall.

Two cautions. First, our technician runs the sound and the microphones, and your team runs the slides. Agree who changes the screen for each category, because that person has to be in the room and follow the running order. Second, music for the entrances and the winners is also a cue. Agree in advance who starts each track and who gives the signal, and tell us during the planning whether you want us to handle it, so we confirm what the technician covers before the day.

## What We Supply and What We Source

-   **From our own inventory:** active speakers, wireless handheld and gooseneck microphones, a lectern, modular stage platforms, stage lighting as described above, a 60 inch LED display and a technician.
-   **Add ons by quote:** a second handheld, extra microphones, a lectern at 50 euros and modular stage platforms at 35 euros per square meter on the MICE Pack, and an extra hour of the technician at 40 euros.
-   **Sourced with partners and suppliers:** anything we do not own, such as a rig, confetti or a video wall, if there is one. We do not promise availability or a price until we have checked.
-   **Not ours:** the script, the host, the trophies, the set design, the catering and the music licensing. Cameras, live streaming, recording and on screen graphics such as lower thirds are not in our own inventory either.

## Planning the Running Order

A ceremony runs on a list, usually called the run of show, so the audiovisual brief is a list too. Give your supplier:

-   The order of the categories and how many winners each has.
-   Where each person stands and how they reach the stage.
-   How many microphones are in use at the same time.
-   Which moments have walk up music and who starts it.
-   The time of the technical rehearsal, if there is one, and the time of the doors. A short rehearsal with the host and one winner at the microphone is the best way to set the levels.

With that, we match your ceremony to a package and a technician for the right hours. The MICE Pack covers up to 6 hours of the technician on site. If the evening is longer, an extra hour is 40 euros.

