## FAQs

### What equipment does an awards ceremony need?

At least a sound system, a microphone for the host, a way for each winner to be heard, light on the stage and a screen or a sign that shows who is next. A technician runs the sound and the microphones. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers a room of up to 120 guests with a 60 inch LED display, a gooseneck and a wireless handheld microphone and a technician for up to 6 hours.

### How many microphones do I need for a ceremony?

One for the host, plus one for the winners, which is either a second handheld that is passed along or a gooseneck microphone on a lectern. The MICE Pack includes one handheld and one gooseneck. A second handheld is an add on by quote, and we say plainly if your format needs more than we own.

### Do you provide stage lighting for an awards ceremony?

Yes, within our own inventory: 2 Eurolite LED KLS-200 light bars, 1 ADJ Encore FRI50Z Fresnel wash light and 1 ADJ Element H6 Pack of 6 wireless uplights. The Eurolite bars run on a foot pedal and the other fixtures are fixed and set up by our crew, with no DMX and no moving heads. A rig or an overhead truss is not in our own inventory, and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one.

### Can you provide confetti or fireworks?

Not from our own inventory. At the awards ceremony of the Billie Jean King Cup 2024 we supplied the lighting and the sound, and the confetti and the fireworks were not ours. If your ceremony needs them, tell us what you have in mind and we check whether a supplier can cover it, if there is one. We do not promise availability or a price until we have checked.
